Q1. What are the key DevOps practices?

Interview Ready Answer

The key DevOps practices are Collaboration, Automation, Continuous
Integration (CI), Continuous Delivery/Deployment (CD), Continuous
Monitoring, and Infrastructure as Code (IaC). These practices help
organizations deliver software faster, improve quality, reduce manual
effort, and increase deployment reliability.

Definition

DevOps practices are the techniques and processes used to implement the
DevOps culture throughout the software development lifecycle.

Purpose

• Improve collaboration.
• Automate repetitive tasks.
• Deliver software faster.
• Improve software quality.
• Reduce deployment failures.
• Detect issues early.
• Ensure consistent infrastructure.

======================================================================

Q2. Explain each DevOps practice briefly.

Interview Ready Answer

1. Collaboration

Development and Operations teams work together throughout the software
development lifecycle. Continuous communication and feedback reduce
misunderstandings and improve software quality.

------------------------------------------------------------

2. Automation

Manual tasks such as building, testing, deployment, and infrastructure
provisioning are automated. This reduces human errors, saves time, and
improves consistency.

------------------------------------------------------------

3. Continuous Integration (CI)

Developers frequently merge code into a shared repository. Every code
change is automatically built and tested to detect integration issues
early.

------------------------------------------------------------

4. Continuous Delivery / Continuous Deployment (CD)

Software is automatically prepared for release or automatically deployed
to production, enabling faster and more reliable software delivery.

------------------------------------------------------------

5. Continuous Monitoring

Applications, servers, and infrastructure are continuously monitored to
identify performance issues, failures, and security problems as early as
possible.

------------------------------------------------------------

6. Infrastructure as Code (IaC)

Infrastructure such as servers, networks, and cloud resources is managed
using configuration files or code instead of manual configuration. This
ensures consistency, repeatability, and easier management.

